From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] libopenbios: ofmem: find claim memory whose 1:1 virtual range is free

A client interface "claim" with an alignment (virt = 0) takes physical
memory from the top of RAM down and maps it 1:1, but it only looks for
free physical memory. If the virtual range at the same address is taken
the claim fails, although free memory with a free virtual range exists
lower down.

On sparc64 the firmware keeps its own virtual range from OFMEM_VIRT_TOP
(0xff000000) to 4 GB, and its .data and .bss at the top of RAM. With
4 GB of RAM the highest free physical memory ends at 0xffe80000, inside
that range, and with more RAM it is above 4 GB. NetBSD 11.1's first claim
(pmap_alloc_bootargs(): OF_claim(NULL, 2 * PAGE_SIZE, PAGE_SIZE))
then fails, and it stops right after its loader:

  qemu-system-sparc64 -M sun4u -m 4096:
    panic: Can't claim two pages of memory.
    Unhandled Exception 0x0000000000000030

Search below ofmem_arch_get_virt_top() (the claims stay below 4 GB, where
they are with less RAM) and, while the virtual range of the area found is
taken, below that area. With up to 3 GB of RAM the first area found has a
free virtual range, as before, and nothing changes.
---
 libopenbios/ofmem_common.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libopenbios/ofmem_common.c b/libopenbios/ofmem_common.c
index 194db15..609692b 100644
--- a/libopenbios/ofmem_common.c
+++ b/libopenbios/ofmem_common.c
@@ -643,10 +643,29 @@ ucell ofmem_claim( ucell addr, ucell size, ucell align )
 			return -1;
 		}
 	} else {
+		ucell max = get_ram_size(), found = -1;
+
 		if( align < PAGE_SIZE )
 			align = PAGE_SIZE;
-		phys = ofmem_claim_phys_( -1, size, align, 0, get_ram_size(), 1 /* reverse */ );
-		virt = ofmem_claim_virt_( phys, size, 0, 0, 0, 0 );
+		/* The memory is mapped 1:1, so its virtual range must be free
+		   too. With RAM up to or beyond ofmem_arch_get_virt_top() the
+		   top of RAM is the firmware's own virtual range: search below
+		   it, and lower down for as long as the virtual range is taken */
+		if( max > ofmem_arch_get_virt_top() )
+			max = ofmem_arch_get_virt_top();
+		while( max >= size ) {
+			found = find_area( align, size, ofmem->phys_range, 0, max, 1 /* reverse */ );
+			if( found == (ucell)-1 || is_free( found, size, ofmem->virt_range ) )
+				break;
+			max = found;
+			found = -1;
+		}
+		phys = -1;
+		virt = -1;
+		if( found != (ucell)-1 ) {
+			phys = ofmem_claim_phys_( found, size, 0, 0, 0, 0 );
+			virt = ofmem_claim_virt_( found, size, 0, 0, 0, 0 );
+		}
 		if( phys == -1 || virt == -1 ) {
 			OFMEM_TRACE("ofmem_claim failed\n");
 			return -1;
